    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d560-a2">

                <pb facs="0690" n="588" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg588"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Wilson to the Minister for Foreign
                        Affairs.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Brussels</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1908-11-06"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">November 6,
                    1908</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge
                    your excellency’s esteemed note of November 6 conveying the information that the
                    royal decree carrying into execution the provisions of article 4 of the treaty
                    of annexation is fixed for issuance on the 15th of November, on which date the
                    Government of the King will assume sovereignty over its colonial
                    possessions.</p>
                <p>Highly appreciating your excellency’s courteous expressions while bringing this
                    important action to my knowledge, I beg leave to advise you that I have
                    immediately transmitted the information to the Government at Washington and
                    asked for instructions therein.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry Lane
                    Wilson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
